    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Ask the parents:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " how they felt about becoming parents; how the delivery went; how the parent feels now; the baby's name; whether the baby stayed w the parent, had skin-to-skin time and breastfed after birth; questions or concerns about caring for the baby."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Prenatal hx:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " maternal conditions (asthma, diabetes, obesity, poor oral health, thyroid dz, chronic ♡ or kidney dz); preg comp (GDM, hypertensive dx); infect (GBS, chorioamnionitis, UTI, HIV, hepatitis B, STIs, toxoplasmosis, CMV); prenatal diagnoses and interventions; maternal meds and supp; tobacco, EToH or drug use; prior adverse preg outcome."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Delivery hx:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " mother's hepatitis B, HIV, GBS, blood group and Rh status; preterm labor or premature rupture of membranes; mode of delivery and instrumentation; meds and anesthesia; episiotomy or lacerations; duration of labor; comp (fever, infect, bleed, preeclampsia incl. HELLP)."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Newborn @ delivery:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " fetal distress; IUGR, macrosomia, birth trauma; gestational age, birth wt and Apgar score; transition problems (resp distress, cyanosis, hypoglycemia, poor feeding, temp instability, jitteriness, lethargy); risk of w.draw from maternal substance use; vit K and eye prophylaxis."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Neonatal course:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " newborn blood type and direct Coombs; vital signs; blood sugar if @ risk; wt loss or gain; feeding (LATCH scores, freq, duration; formula type if ⍉breastfeed); sleep-wake pattern; meconium passage and wet diapers; risk of severe jaundice; anomalies suggesting a need for genetic eval."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Family hx:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " a comprehensive FHx = recommended @ the 1 mo visit."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "ROS — concerns about:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " head shape; eye d/c; ears, nose and throat; breathing; vomiting or spitting, BMs, umbilical stump; genitals or rectum; skin; development (musc strength, mvt of arms or legs, develop concerns)."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
